A||N||20||Haze_Performance||My new 10" sub......||||6||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||08-07-2001||04:01 AM||||Well I have one of AusFiero's subwoofer center console's.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/consolefront_3.jpg"> <BR> <BR>I now have my sub"<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bottom1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/front1_2.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/frontside1.jpg"> <P>Rockford Fosgate Punch HX2 RFD2210 <BR>10" Dual Voice Coil Component Subwoofer <P>dual voice coil design <BR>CONsealer gasket hides mounting screws and provides airtight seal <BR>LXcursion basket features a deep step that keeps the spider from "bottoming out" and distorting your sound. <BR>frequency response 30-200 Hz <BR>power range 150-500 watts RMS (250 watts per voice coil) <BR>peak power 1,000 watts <BR>sensitivity 85 dB SPL <BR>top mount depth 5-7/16" <BR>sealed box volume 0.2-0.75 cubic feet <P><BR>My sub amp is a Fosgate Power 200.<P><BR>I cant wait to hook it all up..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Has anyone installed one of his console's yet? How does it sound?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">   <BR></A><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Click above to visit my website.</B></FONT></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 08-07-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||Monkeyman||08-07-2001||04:37 AM||||Haze--You'll be amazed at the sound!!!  I've had mine hooked up for a few weeks now and it rocks!  I used a Cerwin Vega sub with a Kenwood amp running both my sub and my Kenwood components, all driven by a Sony head unit.  It makes things a little short on elbow room at 1st, but it's surprising how quickly you get used to that.  I have one of Rodneys' super short shifters so I'm guessing that helps some.  Jims' sub box and door speaker pods are one of the best sound values out there for the Fiero.  Too bad more aren't buying them.  Their loss.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||08-07-2001||12:51 PM||||Nice selection on the sub. My friend had two of those in a ported box in his civic. They slammed hard. He had an 800 watt R/F amp running both of them, so I'm sure they could've been hitting even harder. Be careful not to crank it up too much, being right by your ears and all.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">   <P>84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||14
