Z||000012||AusFiero||08-08-2001||08:23 PM||||Well for those asking about the sub boxes I actually have a new design that has ironed out a few things that people was worried about with the first. As I said a while back, an evolving product. I will post some pictures of the new design in its own thread in a while, as I am just finishing up the pictures. Yes I am supposed to be resting, drawing is rest to me. The new design wont be available for about 6 weeks though when the body kit is all out of the way. Maybe sooner but we will see. The new design will be nade out of reinforced fiberglass and actually match into the original intrior better.<P>Keep an eye out for a thread called redesigned subwoofer centre console.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000013||Haze_Performance||08-11-2001||04:19 AM||||Hmmmm. I just had a reality check. The sub weights 14lbs. Do ya think the box will handle it? Also how is the foam/rubber type stuff going to protect the EMC? That magnet has the pull of 10 men. I need some advice before I install it. I would hate to mess up the EMC or the box.<P>TIA <BR>-Haze   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">        <BR></A><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="green"><B>Hello, My name is Haze. I'm the jerk that sits behind you at a traffic light & rattles your <BR>fillings loose with the unnecessarily loud stereo system.</B></FONT></FONT>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 08-11-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000014||AusFiero||08-11-2001||06:53 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B>Hmmmm. I just had a reality check. The sub weights 14lbs. Do ya think the box will handle it? Also how is the foam/rubber type stuff going to protect the EMC? That magnet has the pull of 10 men. I need some advice before I install it. I would hate to mess up the EMC or the box.<P>TIA <BR>-Haze     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>    The box has wood glue, over 50 screws, then your upholstery holding it together Haze. I know from pushing mine to its limit that it can handle it, and some.<BR>    It hasn't affected my ECM  Mine has been in for 6 months now. I don't know many magnets that can pull through 2 layers of rubber and 9 mms of MDF Board. <BR>   Look under the dash of many modern cars and you will see the ECM sitting close to speakers and totally unprotected, bar a thin layer of rubber.<P>For those asking about the sub console boxes. <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>www.auto-alley.com</A>  is back online, only with a few products at present but the boxes are there. For those willing to wait I have redesigned the box to be built in fibreglass and appropriately reinforced in the right places. The body kit is getting finished first. <BR>    The new box is only 1.5" deeper at the base than a standard Fiero console but the cubic capacity has been increased by making it go 4" over the rear "parcel shelf" and putting a different angle on the face of it. It can also use the standard Fiero side vents and the Fiero Cigarette lighter plate. The new one is 0.76 cubic feet of air space. Below is the design. It will also bolt in as a standard console.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/console003.jpg">  <P>Or maybe a dearer version if people want something totally different.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/console001.jpg">  <P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A><p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 08-16-2001).]||202.139.20.3||reg||1
